r['notes']+='\n\n[Blind audit] The hypothesis ending now admits anabélienne/anabélien, and the following low preposition admits dans/des. The three quoted/parenthetical endings filtrations, modéliques, grossières retain the plural as first reading with singular alternatives; agreement grammar does not decide the small terminal returns. These are certainty-only changes, not new material C rows. The de after the inverse limit has a distinct d and e return, with no separate terminal s. The K(pi,1) sign has a bent left foot and curved top return matching the local lowercase pi. Prendre retains its initial p bowl and long descender, subsequent r/e/n and d ascender; no different complete cancelled word is recoverable from its retracing. The extension map has a curved head at the shaft’s endpoint and remains an arrow. The hom before the preposition ends in an attached m return, not a detached s. The lower shorthand has two bars without m arches and remains resolved =. No mathematical check was undertaken.'
